data: {"event": "audit", "answer_final": "**Definition**  \nAn autonomous system is a computational or physical entity capable of perceiving its environment, formulating goal‑directed plans, and executing actions over extended operational horizons without continuous human intervention [[c:0]].\n\n**Taxonomy of Autonomy Levels**  \n\n| Level | Designation | Core Capability (as defined in the sources) |\n|-------|-------------|---------------------------------------------|\n| 0 | No Automation | System provides warnings or momentary intervention; human controls all execution [[c:0]]. |\n| 1 | Driver/Operator Assistance | Executes either steering or acceleration/deceleration using environmental information [[c:0]]. |\n| 2 | Partial Automation | Simultaneously executes multiple sub‑tasks while the human monitors and remains ready to take over [[c:0]]. |\n| 3 | Conditional Automation | Handles all dynamic performance within a defined Operational Design Domain (ODD); human intervenes on request [[c:0]]. |\n| 4 | High Automation | Sustains complete dynamic performance and automated fallback within the ODD even if the human fails to intervene [[c:0]]. |\n| 5 | Full Automation | Provides unconditional automated performance across all environmental and operational conditions manageable by humans [[c:0]]. |\n\n**Architectural Models**  \nCommon architectures for autonomous systems include the Sense‑Plan‑Act (SPA) hierarchy, the subsumption architecture of layered reactive behaviors, and hybrid cognitive architectures that combine fast reflex loops with asynchronous symbolic deliberation [[c:0]].", "claims": [{"claim_id": 0, "text": "An autonomous system is a computational or physical entity capable of perceiving its environment, formulating goal‑directed plans, and executing actions over extended operational horizons without continuous human intervention.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "An autonomous system is a computational or physical entity capable of perceiving its environment, formulating goal-directed plans, and executing actions over extended operational horizons without continuous human intervention.", "note": "Fully supported: Verified by verbatim evidence quote and entity check.", "supported": true, "status": "supported", "coverage": 1.0, "start": 17, "end": 251}, {"claim_id": 1, "text": "System provides warnings or momentary intervention; human controls all execution.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "System provides warnings or momentary intervention; human controls all execution.", "note": "Fully supported: Verified by verbatim evidence quote and entity check.", "supported": true, "status": "supported", "coverage": 1.0, "start": 450, "end": 539}, {"claim_id": 2, "text": "Executes either steering or acceleration/deceleration using environmental information.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "Execution of either steering or acceleration/deceleration using environmental information.", "note": "Audit flagged: unverified entities: Executes.", "supported": false, "status": "partially_supported", "coverage": 0.857, "start": 577, "end": 671}, {"claim_id": 3, "text": "Simultaneously executes multiple sub‑tasks while the human monitors and remains ready to take over.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "Simultaneous execution of multiple sub-tasks with human monitoring and immediate fallback readiness.", "note": "Audit flagged: insufficient quote coverage (36.4% < 60%); unverified entities: Simultaneously.", "supported": false, "status": "partially_supported", "coverage": 0.364, "start": 701, "end": 808}, {"claim_id": 4, "text": "Handles all dynamic performance within a defined Operational Design Domain (ODD); human intervenes on request.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "System handles all aspects of dynamic performance within an Operational Design Domain (ODD); human intervenes upon request.", "note": "Fully supported: Verified by verbatim evidence quote and entity check.", "supported": true, "status": "supported", "coverage": 0.917, "start": 842, "end": 960}, {"claim_id": 5, "text": "Sustains complete dynamic performance and automated fallback within the ODD even if the human fails to intervene.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "System sustains complete dynamic performance and automated fallback within defined ODD even if human fails to intervene.", "note": "Fully supported: Verified by verbatim evidence quote and entity check.", "supported": true, "status": "supported", "coverage": 1.0, "start": 987, "end": 1108}, {"claim_id": 6, "text": "Provides unconditional automated performance across all environmental and operational conditions manageable by humans.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "Unconditional automated performance across all environmental and operational conditions manageable by human operators.", "note": "Fully supported: Verified by verbatim evidence quote and entity check.", "supported": true, "status": "supported", "coverage": 0.8, "start": 1135, "end": 1261}, {"claim_id": 7, "text": "Common architectures for autonomous systems include the Sense‑Plan‑Act (SPA) hierarchy, the subsumption architecture of layered reactive behaviors, and hybrid cognitive architectures that combine fast reflex loops with asynchronous symbolic deliberation.", "citation_ids": [0], "evidence": "1. Sense-Plan-Act (SPA): Classical hierarchical planning through centralized state representations.; 3. Hybrid Cognitive Architectures: Coupling fast reflex loops with asynchronous symbolic deliberation.", "note": "Audit flagged: unverified entities: Common.", "supported": false, "status": "partially_supported", "coverage": 0.625, "start": 1292, "end": 1554}], "removed_claims": [], "conflicts": [], "retractions": [], "confidence": 0.69, "tier_agreement": null, "repaired": true, "sources": [{"source": "ARIA seed note (draft)", "source_type": "okf_graph", "tier": "OKF", "similarity": null, "is_retracted": false, "rank": null, "published": null, "cited": true}, {"source": "Linked via Taxonomy of Autonomous Systems and Operational Boundaries", "source_type": "okf_graph", "tier": "OKF", "similarity": null, "is_retracted": false, "rank": null, "published": null, "cited": false}]}

